        "text": "Strong policy and semiconductor geopolitical story from a primary source (FT)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3622,
        "endIndex": 3861,
        "text": "**What is confirmed:** *The Guardian* reported on 13 November 2026 that logician Jan von Plato (University of Helsinki) used Anthropic’s Claude to process 1,009 pages of Kurt Gödel's 1940s shorthand workbooks (from human transcriptions)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        14,
        15
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3863,
        "endIndex": 3935,
        "text": "Claude generated a 650-page breakdown identifying 663 theorem candidates"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        16,
        15
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3937,
        "endIndex": 4075,
        "text": "Running the statements through the Coq proof assistant formally verified approximately 400 as stated and ~200 with minor parameter repairs"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        16,
